  "question": {
    "text": "A proton collides with a stationary deuteron to form a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>He</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts></math> nucleus. For this reaction to take place, the proton must have a minimum kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. If instead, a deuteron collides with a stationary proton to make a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>He</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts></math> nucleus, then it must have minimum kinetic energy equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>1.5</mtext><mo>&#xA0;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#xA0;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
